{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "name": "outdoor_enclosure_pilot",
  "provenance": "Outdoor wall/pole-mounted electronics enclosure, pilot 50 units. Synthetic enclosure_fixture geometry (not a validated product design). Requirements, not physics: order quantity 50, a 10 K margin between the housing temperature extremes and the conservative route-material service limits, and at least 1 W of supported PCB dissipation. PCB power is swept (1-15 W): two linear solves per candidate (1 W and 15 W, power_sweep mode, radiation off, which is conservative at the hot point) give max_supported_pcb_power_w by superposition, bounded by the component limit on the hotter of board peak and internal air and by the housing service limit less the 10 K margin; the refine tier verifies it with a third solve at that power (0.5 K). Chain: spreadsheet variant -> conformal general-solid mesh -> steady enclosure conduction (docs/enclosure-thermal.md). Environment is normative, not site weather: ETSI EN 300 019-1-4 class 4.1 hot design point (40 degC air, 1120 W/m2 solar, still-air film 2.2 W/(m2*K)) for the solves and its cold point (-33 degC) for the minimum service temperature (data/conditions.json, docs/design-conditions.md). The internal cavity film is the cited conservative low end (1.2 W/(m2*K)). The component limit (85 degC, upper end of the industrial temperature grade) and the isotropic board conductivity (0.26 W/(m*K), the low end of the cited through-plane range, below every cited in-plane value; anisotropy not modelled) are cited conservative DEFAULTS, not product data. The single categorical route lists only compatible MATERIAL__PROCESS__FINISH triples; the finish sets the housing and lid optics. The pc-uv window uses the explicit conservative bound transparent_solar = deposit_incident_in_cavity. PA12 stays a candidate but cannot pass its 10 K cold margin (-40 degC limit vs -33 degC). Replace source_job with an authorized enclosure_fixture job.",
